<Base title="About — Hexfield" description="Why Hexfield exists: connected, readable notes on security fundamentals.">
  <section class="page-intro wrap"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> ABOUT THE PROJECT</div><h1>Understand<br /><em>before you act.</em></h1><p>Hexfield is a growing collection of field notes on the systems that shape offensive security.</p></section>
  <section class="about-body wrap"><div class="about-side">THE IDEA <span>↘</span></div><div class="about-main"><h2>Security gets clearer when the pieces connect.</h2><p>A command is easy to memorize. A system is more useful to understand. Hexfield starts with the relationships between identities, services, protocols, and evidence, then turns those relationships into a practical learning path.</p><p>The free field notes are written for curious learners moving toward OSCP and Red Team work. The planned Academy will add Active Directory practice sets and in depth interview notes. Everything here focuses on fundamentals and authorized practice.</p><div class="about-principles"><div><span>01</span><strong>Build mental models</strong><p>Learn how a system works before memorizing a workflow.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Follow connections</strong><p>Use the roadmap to see how one concept supports the next.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Practice responsibly</strong><p>Apply what you learn only in environments you own or may test.</p></div></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/academy/">Explore the Academy plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</Base>
